		    unifyCodexSessionHistory: "Unified Codex session history",
		    unifyCodexSessionHistoryDescription: `Affects the Codex CLI only: its resume list shows only the current provider's sessions. When enabled, the official subscription runs under the shared "custom" provider id so official and third-party sessions appear in one list. The Codex desktop app can show all sessions since a recent update, so desktop-only users don't need this. You can optionally migrate existing official sessions in (backed up first) and restore them from backup when turning it off. Note: resuming an old session across providers may fail because its encrypted_content reasoning can only be decrypted by the backend that created it.`,
		    codexStackClassicSubagents: "Classic sub-agent tools in aggregation",
		    codexStackClassicSubagentsDescription: "In Codex aggregation mode, a sub-agent whose model comes from a different provider than the main agent may not be able to read its task: the newer Codex sub-agent tools have the main agent's provider encrypt the task, and no other provider can decrypt it. When enabled, every aggregated model uses the classic Codex sub-agent tools, which pass the task as plain text; the trade-off is losing newer features such as followup_task and interrupt_agent. Only affects aggregation mode; restart Codex for the change to take effect.",
		    codexStackClassicSubagentsForcedV2: "Codex config.toml turns on [features] multi_agent_v2, which takes precedence over this setting, so it has no effect.",
		    codexSessionCompression: "Compress old Codex sessions",
		    codexSessionCompressionDescription: "When on, Codex compresses session files that haven't changed for 7 days in the background each time it starts, which saves a lot of disk space. Codex decompresses a session automatically when you continue it. CC Switch still lists and counts compressed sessions; the list just doesn't show a preview of their last reply. This is a Codex feature still under development: Codex shows a notice on every start while it's on. Requires a recent Codex version and takes effect after restarting Codex. Turning it off stops compressing; sessions already compressed stay as they are.",
